WEBVTT

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:08.500
Good morning, everyone.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:20.620
Be patient.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:54.010
I wanted a busy night. Don't worry. I didn't forget you.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.550
Let's try it without biting my fingers this time.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:54.100
It's been a long time. My time is fine. I will see my dream come alive and last. Touch the sky. Gonna hold me down no more. They're not gonna change my mind.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:58.820
We're getting jealous you get more letters from home than anyone on this ship. What's her name? It's nothing like that

00:02:58.820 --> 00:02:59.920
They're from Dr. Luke

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.340
the colleague from the Interspecies Medical Exchange.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:04.970
I didn't know there were humans serving on Denobula.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:05.990
He's the first.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.450
He helped me get settled in when I came to San Francisco.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.150
I'm trying to return the favor.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.380
I had a pen pal once when I was 12, from Brisbane, Australia.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.220
I loved getting her letters.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.950
It was like this little window into distant places

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.770
with strange-sounding names.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.720
The curiosity of an explorer even then.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.590
Are we still on for later?

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.840
Oh, yes. I'm looking forward to it.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.180
If you think you're ready, we can tackle Jerrens today.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.900
I can hardly wait.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.260
My dear Dr. Phlox, it's me again, Jeremy.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:46.620
I hope you're well.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.300
It's been a hell of a week here.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:51.220
Wall-to-wall emergencies and three midnight deliveries.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.900
It's mating season, so you know how that goes.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:56.940
I thought human reproduction was complicated.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:59.980
Your denobulans make us look like single-cell organ...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:08.220
Dear Dr. Lucas, sorry to hear about your difficult week.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.080
I know the rigors of mating season only too well.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:14.320
It might help to bear in mind that a dose of niaxilin

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.320
can be quite effective in separating the two combatants.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.550
It sounds like you've settled into your new living quarters.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.510
That part of the city has some very lively

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.110
cave-in bars along the river.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:25.750
Up here, doc.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.940
We're open all night, if I recall.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:29.980
Please don't.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.890
If you venture inside them unescorted, they can be quite disturbing to the uninitiated.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:39.890
He was trying to reroute a nitrogen valve and the seal blew. How bad is it?

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:49.670
That's superficial. Only first-degree burns.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.160
Malene gel should do the trick.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:59.150
Most of my work is fairly routine. Scrapes and bruises, the occasional emergency.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.820
you'll be pleased to hear that the crew finally seems to be growing accustomed to an alien

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:09.680
doctor on board. I must admit, I wasn't planning to stay this long, but the opportunity to observe

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:15.680
your species on their first deep space venture has proven irresistible. Lieutenant, same seat

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:24.100
for you. Another time, Doctor. I'm due back in the armory. It's a bit daunting at times trying

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:29.790
to socialize with the crew, form friendships, but our profession guarantees that sooner or later

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:36.450
everyone comes to see us it makes interaction quite a bit easier it's just a little gastrointestinal

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:48.160
distress he hasn't met himself lately well you've been feeding him cheese again haven't you you've

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:53.920
got to learn how to say no captain no more dairy products you hear that doctor's orders i never

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:59.480
thought i'd meet a species that forges such intimate bonds with lesser creatures it's surprising the

00:05:59.480 --> 00:05:59.920
things you

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.560
choose to invest your emotions in.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.640
Sorry to bother you with this.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.340
No bother. He was one of my more cooperative patients today.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:14.310
Thanks, Doc. See all the trouble you cause?

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:17.440
I've noticed how the Captain seems to

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.660
anthropomorphize his pet. He even talks

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:21.580
to the creature, although I'm fairly certain

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.020
it has no idea what he's saying.

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:26.130
Then again, I've been known to speak to my

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.410
Pyrethian bat on occasion.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:29.970
We won't be going...

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:37.040
America this time but always I go with you wherever you go understand you go

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:42.940
now Maria no no I stay with you Rebecca no Maria what I do now I do alone I

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:48.190
couldn't do it if you were here if you go then I got you don't you see how it is

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:55.060
whichever one there is we can go if you're bored no no I'd like to stay and

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:59.400
see what happens she won't be disappointed

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:01.310
The ending's classic.

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:03.450
Oh, the film?

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.220
I'm sensing a rising emotional undercurrent in the room.

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:10.250
Curious to see if it culminates in some kind of group response.

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.980
They don't have movies where you come from, do they?

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.880
Well, we had something similar a few hundred years ago,

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:18.660
but they lost their appeal when people discovered

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.300
their real lives were more interesting.

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:26.110
Oh, still, it's nice to take a break from real life

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:27.290
every now and then, don't you think?

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.510
I suppose it is.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:59.560
It's remarkable, Doctor, even fictional characters seem to elicit human compassion.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:03.100
My shipmates have calmly faced any number of dangers,

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:06.280
and yet a simple movie can bring tears to their eyes.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:12.760
Temporal vein.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:13.880
Temporal vein.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:16.220
Internal maxillary.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.180
And what is the maxillary connected to?

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:23.870
Posterior...auricular?

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:24.670
Very good.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:26.390
The external jugular.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.960
Oh, uh, superior...

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:31.120
Vina Cava.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:32.160
And that leads to...

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:32.820
Oh, easy.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:34.890
Receipt of all joy and sadness.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:40.260
Physiologically, it is nothing more than a very efficient pump.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:45.530
Possibly make you people think it is the source of all emotion.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.750
You know, you may know about our cardiopulmonary system.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:51.120
You have a lot to learn about the human art.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:53.460
This is major.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:01.400
I wanted to thank you.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:02.780
It was fun tonight.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:04.040
You're welcome.

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:07.000
Uh, they're showing another one next week.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:08.040
Sunset Boulevard.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:09.920
I think you might like it.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:11.430
I'm sure I will.

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:13.600
Um, see you tomorrow?

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:14.940
Oh, sorry.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:17.760
I didn't know billions don't like to be touched.

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:19.290
It's all right.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.440
I'm trying to shed some of my cultural inhibitions.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:26.840
Oh, in that case, goodnight.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:37.280
Since we were on the subject of mating,

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.960
I think Crewman Cutler may be romantically interested in me.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.480
I can't be certain, however,

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:47.310
the pheromones of human females aren't as potent as Denobulans.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:56.510
The system's nearby.

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.250
There's a Manchara-class planet less than a light year away.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:05.420
The ship's not answering our hails, Captain.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.880
It's definitely pre-warp, sir.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:09.960
Could be unmanned.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:11.900
Maybe a probe of some kind.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:13.460
Any bioscience?

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.020
Two. Very faint.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.140
Bring it into launch bay two.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:33.330
Tell Dr. Phlox he might have a couple of patients.

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:53.120
We found your ship adrift.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.000
We thought we might be able to help.

00:10:57.960 --> 00:10:58.480
Trenakandula, Ta?

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:03.040
Morena Donna?

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.790
I need a little more.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:08.200
I'm Jonathan Archer.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:10.150
You're on the Starship Enterprise.

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:12.750
Kandala von Ganesh.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:16.320
Eureta Vala?

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:20.590
Can you understand me?

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:23.840
Who are you?

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:26.570
Planet.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:27.650
Earth.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.180
We're from Earth.

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:33.580
This is a warp vessel?

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:35.180
Yes.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:41.280
We left Valakis over a year ago, along with three other ships.

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:42.720
Why?

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:46.620
You must have noticed our condition by now.

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:48.520
I detected the illness.

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:51.930
Twelve million of us died the year before we left.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:54.540
You can only imagine how many have died since.

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:58.660
Our doctors can't find a cure, but a more advanced people.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.380
People with warp technology, like you.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.300
Your medical science must be more effective.

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:08.380
You've encountered other warp-capable species.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:12.830
The Mclexa and the Ferengi, they both visited our world.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:15.130
Do you know them?

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:19.280
No.

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:23.620
Are you the ship's doctor?

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:24.600
I am.

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:28.060
People are dying.

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:31.480
Will you allow them to help us?

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:39.180
Any thoughts?

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:44.320
They did come looking for us.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.080
And considering they've already met two other warp-capable species,

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:54.900
the risk of contamination seems acceptable.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:10.160
what you can do. Thank you. If this letter arrives later than usual, Doctor, I hope you'll

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:15.660
forgive me. I've been presented with a rather unusual case involving a pair of alien astronauts.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:20.670
It may not surprise you that they landed in my sickbay through an act of human compassion.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:29.960
I said before...

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:35.620
my duties entail the occasional emergency emergencies it seem come in all shapes and sizes

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:42.960
i was once nearly overwhelmed by 50 patients in a refugee camp on metallis captain archer is now

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:49.400
asking me to take responsibility for over 50 million um

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:28.460
I've noticed you and Kruman Cutler spending a lot of time together.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:29.970
Is there a s***?

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.780
Is there something going on between you two?

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.280
In Denopilun, please.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:37.650
Um...

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:45.830
I believe the word you're searching for is dating.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.130
Well, are you?

00:14:57.930 --> 00:14:58.530
Gundisa.

00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:05.600
There are ways you can tell.

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:20.700
Make physical contact.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.320
Well, she did kiss me on the cheek the other night.

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:26.060
Indenobulan doctor.

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:42.280
I beg your pardon?

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:43.380
Couple.

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:45.910
Cute couple.

00:15:58.740 --> 00:15:59.560
Crowned it out there.

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:02.400
A lot of spacecraft and artificial satellites.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:04.330
Nothing I can't avoid, sir.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.900
But it's in a low orbit, Travis. They're expecting us.

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:14.760
The captain has committed all our resources to helping people he didn't even know existed two days ago.

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.370
Once again, I'm struck by your species' desire to help others.

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:28.420
It seems the more aggressively we treat the illness, the more resistant it becomes.

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:29.910
What's the current rate of infection?

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:34.660
one out of three it's a full-blown epidemic these are in the most advanced

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:41.570
stage you're treating them with a synthetic antibody it's effective at

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:45.520
first but the disease mutates once it moves into the respiratory system

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:49.460
there's no way of controlling it pulmonary failure usually follows in a

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:53.650
few days captain treatment with priaxate should ease the symptoms in the sickest

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:57.550
patients at least temporarily I can easily show the blocky inside of

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:58.710
synthesize as much as they need

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.230
I'll need all of the lab work you have

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:06.150
and case histories of patients in every stage of the disease.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:06.840
Certainly.

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:21.500
Excuse me, we're the ones that brought him here.

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:22.620
Can you tell me how he's doing?

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:28.370
I'm sorry, did you say that again?

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.770
We should assign some crewmen to watch Dr. Flogs and his equipment.

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:38.530
I don't think these people are about to steal anything.

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:43.400
Your experience with lesser civilizations is limited, Captain.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:48.500
You might be surprised what a temptation our technology can be.

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:58.140
Hoshi?

00:17:58.500 --> 00:17:59.960
Captain, the UT can't trans...

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.700
He doesn't speak the same language as you?

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.750
No. He's Menk.

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:10.560
They're not as evolved as Wallachians,

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:11.780
but they're very hard workers.

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:14.250
They're indigenous to this planet?

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:16.380
Is that so strange?

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:19.530
On most of the planets we've encountered,

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:22.040
only one species of humanoids

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.440
survived the evolutionary process.

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:26.480
You two are not from the same planet?

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:28.810
No.

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:33.220
We may look alike, but the similarity ends there.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:36.880
I don't see any Mank patients here. Where are they being treated?

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:38.740
They haven't contracted the disease.

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:41.400
Have you looked into their immunity?

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:43.370
Oh, it was one of the first things we pursued,

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:47.070
but Mank and Wallachian are physiologically incompatible.

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:48.470
Still, it could be significant.

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:50.970
I'd like to see your date on the Mank as well.

00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:52.080
Of course.

00:18:54.090 --> 00:18:56.610
I had meant to transmit this letter by now,

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:59.960
but the Wallachian epidemic has been taking up most of my...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:06.060
time working with the physicians here has been quite fulfilling i suppose it's the reason we

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:12.490
joined the interspecies medical exchange but i worry about falsely raising their hopes despite

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:18.760
captain archer's confidence in me i'm afraid the scale of the disaster may outweigh our best

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:27.300
intentions i've decided to enlist crewman cutler's help in my task so what do they make like have the

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:28.040
a chance to see for yourself.

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:34.220
Trained exobiologist, I'd find your assistance in the field invaluable.

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:35.600
Thank you, doctor.

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:41.400
On a personal note, the affection Krumen Cutler is showing has left me a bit perplexed,

00:19:41.710 --> 00:19:44.490
so I've decided to discuss it with the one person on board

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:47.350
who might understand the complexities of the situation.

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:48.990
That's impossible.

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:50.780
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:55.100
My teeth were sealed with a trifluorinate compound 23 years ago.

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:58.910
Well, normal wear and tear has allowed some decay to sneak in.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:19:59.390
See for yourself.

00:20:00.188 --> 00:20:00.688
Hmm?

00:20:01.692 --> 00:20:04.012
there on your anterior tricuspid.

00:20:09.148 --> 00:20:12.448
I'm sure you have more pressing concerns. I'll come back later.

00:20:12.448 --> 00:20:14.788
I'm waiting for the computer to analyze some tissue samples.

00:20:15.388 --> 00:20:16.988
It'll only take a moment to repair.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:27.940
open please.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:30.840
I don't know.

00:20:36.812 --> 00:20:37.692
You've lived.

00:20:37.964 --> 00:20:39.964
Among humans for quite some time now sub commander. I'm

00:20:40.684 --> 00:20:41.164
Curious.

00:20:42.124 --> 00:20:44.444
Have you ever known them to mate outside their species?

00:20:44.844 --> 00:20:45.404
Uh-uh.

00:20:45.932 --> 00:20:46.432
There it is.

00:20:53.228 --> 00:20:57.068
Are you asking out of personal interest or scientific curiosity?

00:20:58.636 --> 00:20:59.396
Both, I suppose.

00:20:59.632 --> 00:20:59.972
There's it.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:04.290
I've become close with, I think she's attracted to me.

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:08.760
In my experience, humans lack the emotional maturity

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:10.200
for interspecies relationships.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.960
They tend to be easily infatuated

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:14.420
with things they find new.

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:19.900
this crewman may simply be satisfying her curiosity at your expense.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:29.890
Subcommander T'Pol has a very pragmatic view of the universe.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:36.180
I admire her logic, although she lacks the instinctiveness that a more emotional response can provide.

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:39.690
Somehow, I find this unsettling.

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:42.590
Ah, that wasn't so bad.

00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:47.550
Thanks for your insights.

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:50.000
Be careful.

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:50.320
Okay.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:04.900
You asked to see me, Captain.

00:22:05.060 --> 00:22:07.980
I've just gotten a call from the director of the clinic.

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:10.550
He's eager to hear if you've made any progress.

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:22.860
I've developed a medication to ease the symptoms of the disease.

00:22:31.948 --> 00:22:35.668
This epidemic isn't being caused by a virus or bacteria.

00:22:37.004 --> 00:22:39.724
The proteins that bind to their chromosomes are deteriorating.

00:22:40.812 --> 00:22:42.152
Their illness is genetic.

00:22:42.924 --> 00:22:44.924
It's been going on for thousands of years, but the...

00:22:45.484 --> 00:22:48.604
rate of mutation has accelerated over the last few generations.

00:22:50.252 --> 00:22:51.632
based on my projections.

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:54.340
the Ibalachians will be extinct.

00:22:54.412 --> 00:22:55.652
in less than two centuries.

00:22:58.732 --> 00:22:59.732
better than that.

00:23:04.764 --> 00:23:05.764
What about a cure?

00:23:07.132 --> 00:23:10.452
Genetic abnormalities on this level are very difficult to reverse.

00:23:11.900 --> 00:23:12.740
but not impossible.

00:23:14.076 --> 00:23:14.576
No.

00:23:15.004 --> 00:23:17.644
I still believe the main community could be the key to a cure.

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:20.580
I plan to study them in more detail.

00:23:21.276 --> 00:23:22.276
Take all the time you need.

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:43.240
and I began to practice medicine.

00:23:43.468 --> 00:23:46.968
I had no idea it would take me on journeys to other worlds.

00:23:47.404 --> 00:23:51.164
Every species I encounter allows me to explore a new physiology.

00:23:51.788 --> 00:23:56.768
At the moment, I find myself in the enviable position of studying two humanoids from the same planet.

00:23:57.452 --> 00:23:59.452
It's a rare and exciting opportunity.

00:24:02.780 --> 00:24:07.240
Tell them we'd like to run some tests, take samples of their blood, it will be completely

00:24:07.240 --> 00:24:07.640
painless.

00:24:16.540 --> 00:24:21.270
He says they'd be happy to help.

00:24:22.130 --> 00:24:27.140
As fascinating as the two species are from a biological standpoint, it's their ability

00:24:27.140 --> 00:24:29.240
to coexist that intrigues me the most.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.660
The Malachians are highly evolved, technologically advanced,

00:24:33.330 --> 00:24:36.330
while the Menk are relatively primitive, by comparison.

00:24:37.530 --> 00:24:41.190
I'm surprised the two seem to be living side by side, peacefully.

00:24:44.580 --> 00:24:45.220
Pradumata.

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:48.650
Pradukat mta kumumba.

00:25:06.620 --> 00:25:08.340
He wants to know what you're doing.

00:25:09.560 --> 00:25:12.290
Have you learned enough, Meng, to explain a molecular bioscan?

00:25:13.940 --> 00:25:24.580
Doctor, um, Isataproku, Kuvalaki, what'd you say?

00:25:25.550 --> 00:25:27.310
Told him the doctor was looking inside of him.

00:25:32.950 --> 00:25:33.830
Thank you.

00:25:34.490 --> 00:25:35.330
Teak, teak.

00:25:36.410 --> 00:25:36.790
Nanda.

00:25:39.200 --> 00:25:39.580
You're welcome.

00:25:42.260 --> 00:25:44.870
Nik, razata, food.

00:25:45.940 --> 00:25:46.900
Did he just say food?

00:25:47.900 --> 00:25:49.260
Razata, food.

00:25:49.500 --> 00:25:50.990
Have you been teaching him English?

00:25:51.210 --> 00:25:53.930
No, he must have picked it up by listening to us.

00:25:54.190 --> 00:25:56.330
Perhaps we found an assistant calm officer.

00:25:59.770 --> 00:25:59.930
No.

00:26:03.540 --> 00:26:11.980
I haven't seen any crops or lye stonks, I wonder where they get this.

00:26:18.740 --> 00:26:23.600
He says the soil here isn't good for planting.

00:26:30.670 --> 00:26:33.150
The Wallachians don't let them live where the land is fertile.

00:26:33.930 --> 00:26:43.000
The Wallachians give them whatever they need, food, clothing, medicine.

00:26:45.800 --> 00:26:51.730
He says the Wallachians are good to them, they protect them.

00:27:02.560 --> 00:27:04.860
Despite the Manks' insistence that they're treated well,

00:27:04.980 --> 00:27:07.560
my human crewmates seem to see things differently.

00:27:09.340 --> 00:27:09.660
Tick, tick.

00:27:13.620 --> 00:27:18.500
They think the Mank are being exploited by the Balochians,

00:27:18.990 --> 00:27:21.490
so their first instinct is to rise to their defense,

00:27:22.220 --> 00:27:26.040
despite the fact that the Mank don't appear to need or want a defender.

00:27:28.070 --> 00:27:28.510
Wait a moment.

00:27:35.280 --> 00:27:36.830
Why'd he do?

00:27:37.720 --> 00:27:39.520
He's grouped the samples together by family.

00:27:40.230 --> 00:27:44.140
Cross-referenced by bloodlines and marriage,

00:27:44.200 --> 00:27:46.140
if I'm interpreting the color codes correctly.

00:27:48.310 --> 00:27:48.790
Tick-tick.

00:27:50.470 --> 00:27:53.250
On the surface, the mank appear to be a primitive species,

00:27:54.200 --> 00:27:56.080
unsophisticated even by human standards.

00:27:56.460 --> 00:27:57.290
No offense.

00:27:57.770 --> 00:27:59.950
But their abilities appear to have been underestimated.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:08.560
even by myself seems like a vacation I didn't keep remembering why we were here

00:28:08.560 --> 00:28:15.910
I'm gonna help Laura finish packing up he's back on duty at the hospital in an

00:28:15.910 --> 00:28:28.120
hour this really doesn't bother you what where the Wallachians treat them why

00:28:29.590 --> 00:28:29.850
should it

00:28:30.890 --> 00:28:34.250
On most worlds, with two humanoid species, one would have driven the other to extinction.

00:28:35.180 --> 00:28:39.160
Here, they've developed a symbiotic relationship that seems to work quite well.

00:28:39.500 --> 00:28:41.100
They force the men to live in compounds.

00:28:41.500 --> 00:28:42.880
They treat them almost like pets.

00:28:43.780 --> 00:28:44.960
Their culture is different.

00:28:45.220 --> 00:28:46.400
It's their way.

00:28:47.730 --> 00:28:48.510
Doesn't make it right.

00:28:51.090 --> 00:28:52.010
Are you married, Krumen?

00:28:55.770 --> 00:28:56.590
I would have told you.

00:28:57.110 --> 00:28:57.770
I'm married.

00:28:59.470 --> 00:28:59.850
You are.

00:29:00.510 --> 00:29:01.030
Three times.

00:29:02.510 --> 00:29:04.760
So you have two ex-wives?

00:29:05.160 --> 00:29:07.880
I have three current wives, and they each have two husbands.

00:29:08.520 --> 00:29:09.720
Not counting myself.

00:29:11.180 --> 00:29:14.820
Is that considered normal for denobilians?

00:29:15.750 --> 00:29:16.090
Quite.

00:29:16.310 --> 00:29:21.770
Why are you telling me this?

00:29:23.160 --> 00:29:27.820
I've been getting certain signals from you that suggest you may be interested in a romantic relationship with me.

00:29:31.150 --> 00:29:35.430
Unless I misinterpreted those signals.

00:29:36.730 --> 00:29:42.950
You didn't. I still don't know why you're telling me this.

00:29:44.760 --> 00:29:47.020
You need to know that my culture is different.

00:29:47.720 --> 00:29:48.480
That doesn't matter.

00:29:49.180 --> 00:29:52.950
It doesn't. This culture is different. That seems to matter to you a great deal.

00:29:54.290 --> 00:29:59.970
Fox, as far as your extent...

00:30:00.600 --> 00:30:05.560
goes, I'm not interested in becoming wife number four.

00:30:05.740 --> 00:30:08.850
I just want to be your friend.

00:30:13.040 --> 00:30:14.140
What do you mean by friend?

00:30:16.470 --> 00:30:17.850
Let's just see where it goes.

00:30:46.440 --> 00:30:57.710
glad you could come. It was no problem. How are you feeling? The medication you gave us helps with

00:30:57.710 --> 00:30:58.130
the pain.

00:31:02.330 --> 00:31:03.750
Your prognosis hasn't changed.

00:31:06.300 --> 00:31:07.740
We're trying to do something about that.

00:31:09.170 --> 00:31:10.890
I have a lot of faith in Dr. Flox.

00:31:11.070 --> 00:31:17.710
I wanted to thank you for getting me home

00:31:17.710 --> 00:31:18.770
before it was too late.

00:31:21.370 --> 00:31:23.210
It took us a year to get out to where you found us.

00:31:23.210 --> 00:31:24.370
You brought us home in a day.

00:31:25.600 --> 00:31:28.560
We started out in ships, very similar to yours.

00:31:30.600 --> 00:31:33.440
Someday you'll be traveling just as fast as we are.

00:31:35.280 --> 00:31:36.600
Someday may not be soon enough.

00:31:38.490 --> 00:31:39.790
If your doctor can't help us,

00:31:39.990 --> 00:31:43.830
we'll need to keep searching for others that can.

00:31:47.660 --> 00:31:48.540
We need warp drive.

00:31:51.380 --> 00:31:52.660
A million more of us will die

00:31:52.660 --> 00:31:54.460
before our next ship even leaves this system.

00:31:55.480 --> 00:31:56.840
With warp engines, we won't have to wait

00:31:56.840 --> 00:31:57.900
for people to find us.

00:31:58.940 --> 00:31:59.960
We can seek help on-

00:32:02.430 --> 00:32:05.450
You may not find that everyone you meet wants to help you.

00:32:07.420 --> 00:32:10.050
Still, we have to try.

00:32:19.290 --> 00:32:22.180
It's Phlox, Captain. We've collected all the samples.

00:32:22.380 --> 00:32:26.180
I'll meet you at the shuttle pod. Archer out.

00:32:54.320 --> 00:32:58.190
We've received 29 hails in the past two hours.

00:33:00.670 --> 00:33:08.550
Apparently word of our arrival has spread quickly. Other clinics are requesting help. Two orbital spacecraft approaches while you were on the planet.

00:33:10.500 --> 00:33:15.190
Mistakenly believes that we already had a cure. We had to turn them away.

00:33:40.590 --> 00:33:42.110
The Slokeans want our warp technology.

00:33:45.030 --> 00:33:45.670
What did you tell them?

00:33:48.200 --> 00:33:48.940
I'd think about it.

00:33:50.710 --> 00:33:50.990
And?

00:33:53.290 --> 00:33:55.150
Safe to say I know where you stand on the subject.

00:33:56.880 --> 00:33:59.960
Even if you give them our reactor schematics, they don't...

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:02.580
They don't have the technical expertise to build a warp engine.

00:34:05.100 --> 00:34:06.860
They have no experience working with antimatter.

00:34:09.060 --> 00:34:15.380
I doubt they even realize how dangerous it is already.

00:34:16.260 --> 00:34:17.680
Then your decision shouldn't be difficult.

00:34:21.160 --> 00:34:24.620
We could stay and help them.

00:34:27.730 --> 00:34:29.810
The Vulcans stayed to help Earth 90 years ago.

00:34:31.880 --> 00:34:32.580
We're still there.

00:34:37.450 --> 00:34:43.990
I never thought I'd say this, but I'm beginning to understand how the Vulcans must have felt.

00:35:20.920 --> 00:35:23.080
Captain. Looks like I'm not the only one.

00:35:25.660 --> 00:35:29.980
Well, yeah. Tobelins fire very little.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:35.130
rest unless you count our annual hibernation cycle am I gonna be without

00:35:35.130 --> 00:35:45.360
my doctor this winter only for six days maybe I'll join you any progress the

00:35:49.410 --> 00:35:56.020
research has been challenging to say the least look you're a doctor have you

00:35:56.020 --> 00:35:56.560
found a cure

00:36:04.510 --> 00:36:08.390
Even if I could find one, I'm not sure it would be ethical.

00:36:11.760 --> 00:36:15.620
We'd be interfering with an evolutionary process that has been going on for thousands of years.

00:36:18.600 --> 00:36:21.180
Every time you treat an illness, you're interfering.

00:36:22.270 --> 00:36:23.190
That's what doctors do.

00:36:25.560 --> 00:36:26.800
You're forgetting about the mink.

00:36:28.410 --> 00:36:28.970
About the mink?

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:34.620
I've been studying their genome as well, and I've seen evidence of increasing intelligence,

00:36:35.310 --> 00:36:37.190
motor skills, linguistic abilities.

00:36:37.330 --> 00:36:41.340
Unlike the Wallachians, they appear to be in the process of an evolutionary awakening.

00:36:42.600 --> 00:36:48.630
It may take millennia, but the Mank have the potential to become the dominant species

00:36:48.630 --> 00:36:49.350
on this planet.

00:36:51.050 --> 00:36:54.170
And that won't happen as long as the Wallachians are around?

00:36:55.200 --> 00:36:59.360
If the Mank are to flourish, they need an opportunity to survive on their own.

00:37:00.320 --> 00:37:08.220
What are you suggesting? We choose one species over the other?

00:37:09.200 --> 00:37:12.850
All I'm saying is that we let nature make the choice.

00:37:13.460 --> 00:37:15.590
The hell with nature. You're a doc.

00:37:16.920 --> 00:37:19.600
You have a moral obligation to help people who are suffering.

00:37:19.780 --> 00:37:24.180
I'm also a scientist, and I'm obligated to consider the larger issues.

00:37:26.120 --> 00:37:29.640
35,000 years ago, your species coexisted with other humanoids, isn't that correct?

00:37:31.050 --> 00:37:31.410
Go ahead.

00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:35.390
What if an alien race had interfered

00:37:35.390 --> 00:37:38.310
and given the Neanderdals an evolutionary advantage?

00:37:39.810 --> 00:37:41.190
Fortunately for you, they didn't.

00:37:42.240 --> 00:37:44.140
I appreciate your perspective on all of this,

00:37:44.200 --> 00:37:47.360
but we're talking about something that might happen,

00:37:48.450 --> 00:37:51.360
might happen thousands of years from now.

00:37:53.640 --> 00:37:54.520
They've asked for our help.

00:37:57.020 --> 00:37:59.970
I am not prepared to walk away based on...

00:38:00.060 --> 00:38:06.670
Theory evolution is more than a theory it is a fundamental scientific principle forgive me for saying so

00:38:06.670 --> 00:38:15.860
I believe your compassion for these people is affecting your judgment my compassion guides my judgment captain can you find a cure

00:38:30.800 --> 00:38:39.980
already have. Two days ago, when we first discovered the alien shuttle, I had no idea

00:38:39.980 --> 00:38:45.680
that I'd be facing a dilemma of this magnitude. For the first time, I find myself in conflict

00:38:45.680 --> 00:38:53.020
with my captain. He is my captain, and he's placed a great deal of trust in me. I believe

00:38:53.020 --> 00:38:58.340
I owe him the same, that he's willing to look beyond his sympathy for these poor people.

00:39:07.930 --> 00:39:16.420
Doctor, I'm going down to the Wallachian hospital.

00:39:17.690 --> 00:39:23.970
Sir, go against all my principles if I didn't ask you to reconsider what's...

00:39:23.970 --> 00:39:28.720
I have reconsidered. I spent the whole night reconsidering.

00:39:30.160 --> 00:39:32.640
And what I've decided goes against all my principles.

00:39:38.120 --> 00:39:42.840
Someday, my people are going to come up with some sort of a doctrine.

00:39:43.870 --> 00:39:46.530
Something that tells us what we can and can't do out here.

00:39:47.050 --> 00:39:48.430
Should and shouldn't do.

00:39:50.650 --> 00:39:54.750
But until somebody tells me that they've drafted that directive,

00:39:57.600 --> 00:39:59.860
I'm going to have to remind myself every day.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:03.840
that we didn't come out here to play God.

00:40:04.020 --> 00:40:08.660
I'd like to thank Dr. Lucas

00:40:08.660 --> 00:40:11.460
that if I'd had a chance to talk to you face-to-face,

00:40:11.580 --> 00:40:14.730
you'd have never let me even consider withholding my findings.

00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:19.710
I'm ashamed to say I almost dipped just that.

00:40:22.400 --> 00:40:28.960
Phlox tells me this medicine will help ease the symptoms for a decade.

00:40:30.028 --> 00:40:30.588
Maybe more.

00:40:34.252 --> 00:40:35.512
A lot can happen in that time.

00:40:37.388 --> 00:40:40.608
I wouldn't be surprised if you developed a cure on your own.

00:40:41.132 --> 00:40:41.972
And if we don't.

00:40:45.932 --> 00:40:49.252
As a warp-capable starship, our chances would be greatly improved.

00:40:57.932 --> 00:40:58.932
I'm sorry.

00:41:04.570 --> 00:41:10.280
This will give you detailed instructions on how to synthesize more of the medicine.

00:41:10.320 --> 00:41:14.510
We appreciate everything you've done.

00:41:18.930 --> 00:41:29.430
If I hadn't trusted him to make the right choice, I'd have been no better than the Vulcan diplomats who held your species back because they felt you couldn't make proper decisions on your own.

00:41:30.636 --> 00:41:33.336
I came very close to misjudging, Jonathan Archer.

00:41:35.756 --> 00:41:37.876
But this incident has helped me gain.

00:41:38.988 --> 00:41:39.988
a new respect for him.

00:41:42.252 --> 00:41:44.032
Happiness and health to you, doctor.

00:41:46.252 --> 00:41:47.092
Dedicated colleague.

00:41:48.556 --> 00:41:49.056
vlogs.

00:41:55.276 --> 00:41:56.276
You wanted to see me?

00:41:57.164 --> 00:41:57.664
Please.

00:42:00.090 --> 00:42:00.890
or Dr. Lucas.

00:42:02.570 --> 00:42:03.710
Go out first thing in the morning.

00:42:06.220 --> 00:42:06.960
Everything all right?

00:42:08.740 --> 00:42:09.480
Fine, fine.

00:42:09.620 --> 00:42:15.620
The past few days have been, uh, maxing.

00:42:17.370 --> 00:42:20.820
Well, my advice, get out of sickbay.

00:42:23.460 --> 00:42:25.370
Yes, that's your right.

00:42:27.560 --> 00:42:27.840
Good night.

00:42:30.572 --> 00:42:30.892
Good night.

00:42:43.308 --> 00:42:44.308
to Krummen Cutler.

00:42:45.708 --> 00:42:46.148
Go ahead.

00:42:47.308 --> 00:42:48.068
I, uh...

00:42:48.396 --> 00:42:50.396
No, it's short notice, but...

00:42:51.692 --> 00:42:53.852
I was wondering if you might like to join me for a little...

00:42:54.476 --> 00:42:55.376
back in the mess hall.

00:42:57.484 --> 00:42:59.044
I could use, yeah.

00:43:00.316 --> 00:43:01.276
friend right about now.

00:43:02.716 --> 00:43:03.556
10 minutes?

00:43:04.540 --> 00:43:04.900
Thank you.

00:43:18.652 --> 00:43:18.952
dreams.
